  "id": "COMPOUND:31777 - PROTEIN:6020",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Tatridin B may interact with PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1 through a series of molecular targets. Specifically, Tatridin B is implicated in targeting the Ectonucleotide pyrophosphatase/phosphodiesterase family member 6, which in turn is a target of Quassin and 9-Isovaleroxy Balanophonin. These compounds are all part of a broader class of molecules that may exert their effects by modulating the activity of the CDC2L1 kinase. The final scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, suggesting that Tatridin B may act as a modulator or inhibitor of the kinase pathway, potentially through the regulation of the Ectonucleotide pyrophosphatase/phosphodiesterase family member 6. The evidence is consistent across multiple pathways, highlighting a possible mechanism involving the regulation of kinase activity through the targeting of this enzyme. However, the exact mechanism by which Tatridin B influences the kinase remains to be fully elucidated, and further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional role of Tatridin B in this context.",
